Venetium 0030 - on Windows ARM32 the sandbox no longer claims win32k lockdown (no fake-GDI interceptions).

BATCH-ARM-FIX-2, his decision (2026-10-04, after review wf_8ca010d1-e4a: "Add 0030 now").

Venetium 0029 creates sandboxed children on ARM32 without PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_MITIGATION_POLICY (Windows 10 build 15035 ARM32
refuses that attribute), so WIN32K_SYSTEM_CALL_DISABLE cannot take effect in the renderer and the services (storage service).
Their sandbox config still asked for it, though, and with the flag set:
- the broker installs its fake-GDI interceptions (ProcessMitigationsWin32KDispatcher: GdiDllInitialize returns success without
  initialising gdi32, GetStockObject returns null, RegisterClassW pretends success);
- base::win::IsUser32AndGdi32Available() reads the real process policy, finds win32k usable, and sends renderer code down its
  user32/gdi32 paths.
Upstream never ships that combination. (kWinSboxNoFakeGdiInit is disabled by default, so the fake-GDI rules are added on 15035,
which maps to RS1.)

1 file:
- sandbox/policy/win/sandbox_win.cc: SandboxWin::AddWin32kLockdownPolicy() returns SBOX_ALL_OK at once under #if defined(_M_ARM),
  without setting MITIGATION_WIN32K_DISABLE or SetFakeGdiInit(); its body is unchanged under #else. Both callers (the renderer in
  sandbox_win.cc and kService / kServiceWithJit in utility_sandbox_delegate_win.cc) go through it. Every other architecture is
  unchanged.

Effect on ARM32: renderers and services run with user32/gdi32 usable and no win32k interceptions, as they do with --no-sandbox
(device runs 3 and 4 started renderer and storage-service processes that way). No further protection is lost: win32k lockdown was
already gone at launch with 0029. The config is now truthful, so chrome://sandbox no longer lists win32k lockdown for those
processes on ARM32.

NOT MEASURED: the device run (renderer and storage service under the sandbox).

diff --git a/sandbox/policy/win/sandbox_win.cc b/sandbox/policy/win/sandbox_win.cc
index 9ec89be..14b6984 100644
--- a/sandbox/policy/win/sandbox_win.cc
+++ b/sandbox/policy/win/sandbox_win.cc
@@ -750,6 +750,15 @@ ResultCode SandboxWin::AddAppContainerPolicy(TargetConfig* config,
 // static
 ResultCode SandboxWin::AddWin32kLockdownPolicy(TargetConfig* config) {
   DCHECK(!config->IsConfigured());
+#if defined(_M_ARM)
+  // Venetium 0030: on Windows ARM32 sandboxed children are created without
+  // the mitigation-policy attribute (Venetium 0029: build 15035 refuses it),
+  // so win32k lockdown cannot take effect there. Do not claim it either: with
+  // the flag set the broker would still install its fake-GDI interceptions
+  // (gdi32 initialisation faked) in a process whose win32k works. Renderers
+  // and services then use user32/gdi32 as they do with --no-sandbox.
+  return SBOX_ALL_OK;
+#else
   MitigationFlags flags = config->GetProcessMitigations();
   // Check not enabling twice. Should not happen.
   DCHECK_EQ(0U, flags & MITIGATION_WIN32K_DISABLE);
@@ -765,6 +774,7 @@ ResultCode SandboxWin::AddWin32kLockdownPolicy(TargetConfig* config) {
     return config->SetFakeGdiInit();
   }
   return SBOX_ALL_OK;
+#endif  // defined(_M_ARM)
 }
 
 // static
